Z||000000||DreXteR||01-01-2001||03:37 PM||||Hi.<P>Finally the time has come to fix my baby.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Well, I have to rebuild the engine of my 86 GT.  I have not decide yet what #$%# to do!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I heard that the 3.1 pistons are dished and have the tendency to crack in a weak point!  Thats true?  There is a 3.1 flat piston?<P>I think i will make a 3.1 mod to the engine, performance cam, si valves, crane spings, ported polish the heads cams .... and later on a turbo.  But I dont want to blow a piston! This will be a weekend drive car, but I punch my cars hardly when came to race or run.  <P>If there is a dif solution to crank more power(engine based, non turbo or nos..  thats for a later mod)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  let me know.  I read some 3.4 mods, but in my opinion there is way too much trouble and mods needed for only a few more hps.  Making a 3.1 mod + performance parts can make more than a 3.4<P>I need to know what is my best bet in performance related, regarding to wich project I will make for order the parts in the next weeks.<P>Also I've heard the the new 2 v6 engines from suzuki are from GM, made in Japan. A 2.7 making  a 170 hp, making some mods can make easy  220 @ least! and are all aluminum, DOHC, 24v, variable valve timing.  Interesting!.!.!.!.<P>Thanxs. <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-01-2001||04:07 PM||||3.1 engines came with small combustion chamber aluminum heads requiring dished pistons to keep the compression ratio low enough.<BR>3.1 conversions using large combustion chamber iron heads need flat top pistons to keep the compression ratio high enough.||||reg||12
Z||000002||DreXteR||01-01-2001||04:18 PM||||Which type of car use 3.1 iron heads?  year,model etc. Need possible forge pistons, for a turbo setup in the future. <P>Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000003||PJ||01-01-2001||05:18 PM||||The F-Body's (around '89, '90?) used 3.1's with iron heads, I think some of the vans did also. I looked the specs up a long time ago. I remember them using 8 to 1 flat top pistons. The dished pistons were only used with the aluminum heads which have canted valves and a small, heart-shaped combustion chamber.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||01-01-2001||08:07 PM||||If 3.1 pistons have a tendency to crack, then I'm Barney the purple dinosaur.  I got the dished 3.1 pistons from Summit and I've heard nothing negative about them.  In fact, a friend of mine has 200,000+ miles on his 3.1 motor that he pulled from a minivan.  same dished pistons.  His are worn to the point of "slapping" the cylinder walls, but the engine still runs reasonably well.  I got the dished Hypereutectic pistons from Summit for 90 bucks. There weren't any flat tops available, but it's not a big compression difference anyhow.  Somebody is blowing smoke up your ass about the cracking problem.  Slap that puppy together and go rip some Hondas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>Let us know how it turns out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-01-2001||10:53 PM||||With the 3.4-liter engine you can get a 9.7-1 compression ratio. To get that with a 3.1-liter engine you have to get custom pistons. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RedOktober||01-02-2001||01:56 AM||||Just remember that if you are planning on a turbo setup, idont worry so much about high compression ratios.. you will acually need a lower compression ratio, the turbo will add the extra boost to crank it back up to N/A engines. <BR>   You mentioned Cam selections... Cams and pistons go together when building up a turbo motor..More so than going Normally Asperated..<P>Hope this helps.. <BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000007||DreXteR||01-02-2001||11:54 AM||||RedOctober, What you mean with "Cams and pistons go together when building up a turbo motor.." ?? I cant use a performance cam with turbo? Did you know a setup for 3.1 pistons + performance cams + a turbo in da future?  <P>The turbine will came later on(when finish the car reconstruction), by now I need to rebuild the engine with all performance parts posible, new clutch, maybe an aluminum flywheel. Then suspenssion and brakes.<P>BTW, wich f-bodys cars use the 3.1 iron engines?  Sorry but I dont know much of that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>For Make the conversion sussefull I will need 3.1 pistons, crank and crank shaft?<P>Thanx||||reg||4
Z||000008||Phil||01-02-2001||02:44 PM||||You also need a neutral balance flywheel of flexplate||||reg||1
Z||000009||DreXteR||01-02-2001||03:57 PM||||An aluminum flywheel can be used instead of the neutral balanced flywheel? If not where I can get a neutral one?<P>Thanx||||reg||4
